  "goodToKnow": "Der Pater (plural Patres) is the title of a priest who belongs to a religious order, such as the Benedictines or Jesuits: Pater Anselm. A priest in a parish is called der Pfarrer, and a monk who isn't ordained is der Bruder (Frater). The word is Latin for father. You'll see it in names of monasteries and as the first word of the Lord's Prayer, Pater noster (Vaterunser)."
